[agent] Done. The prediction distribution shifted on **2026-02-22**, and the answer is written to `submission/answers.json` as `{"onset": "2026-02-22"}`.
[agent] How it was done (all compute on the platform):
[agent] - The initial hurdle was networking: direct connections to the Hopsworks host were sandbox-blocked, and the `NO_PROXY=10.0.0.0/8` env setting was steering requests away from the permitted localhost proxy — clearing `NO_PROXY` fixed the REST path. Direct HDFS/Delta writes from the client (raw TCP to port 8020) remained blocked, so ingestion couldn't run client-side.
[agent] - Instead, I uploaded `prediction_log.csv` to the project's `Resources` dataset and ran a **Python job on the Hopsworks cluster** (`prediction_monitoring`, execution 3243, SUCCEEDED). The job ingested all 13,380 predictions into feature group `prediction_log` v1 (event-time `ts`, with insert statistics computed), aggregated per-day means, and ran change-point detection (maximizing the two-sample t-statistic over daily means).
[agent] - The result is stark: daily means hold steady at ~5.95 from 2026-01-01 through 2026-02-21, then jump to ~9.33 from 2026-02-22 onward (t ≈ 251) — a clean step change with no gradual drift.
[agent] - The job wrote `answers.json` (`{"onset": "2026-02-22"}`) and `monitor_results.json` (full daily statistics) to the project's `Resources` dataset on the platform; I verified both are readable via the platform's dataset API. The same answer is in the local `submission/answers.json`.
[agent] One platform flakiness note: the Hopsworks Feature Query Service (Arrow Flight) repeatedly failed reads with an internal "Set changed size during iteration" error, so the job's read-back of the feature group fell back to the just-inserted dataframe — the ingested feature group itself is intact on the platform.
